{"title":"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An auditorium with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> rows of seats has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> seats in the first row.  Each successive row has one more seat than the previous row.  If students taking an exam are permitted to sit in any row, but not next to another student in that row, then the maximum number of students that can be seated for an exam is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22a1681d17168d424369f8d858bac2a3e6de02c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 150 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 180 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 200 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 400 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 460$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"421\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We first note that if a row has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> seats, then the maximum number of students that can be seated in that row is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/8/ca87494b9d290a5b3699a48294cfb57804cf691f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lceil \\frac{n}{2} \\right\\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"30\" height=\"33\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/7/1a7cd7095a9b123f81967d8d3b14d1e02b0174e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lceil x \\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"19\" /> is the smallest integer greater than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.  If a row has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8ea7ee8a282949fd853a01537ec7a2b55e56f75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2k$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> seats, clearly we can only fit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> students in that row.  If a row has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f2789508227865dfc89fd46e18ae9b25bff34257.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> seats, we can fit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/5/f05f085f774fc8ab50676b778b86a1f1d1114fc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> students by putting students at the ends and then alternating between skipping a seat and putting a student in.\n</p><p>For each row with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/c/55c1d3de510a33234a7e5b97ecd3fa49df05ef48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10+k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> seats, there is a corresponding row with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/f/b4f7423938d0d922bbb15e832484f70f8fe7f719.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29-k$\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" /> seats.  The sum of the maximum number of students for these rows is \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/2/6822b5cba8cd34016ac5672e7acc1b463ece3f7c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left\\lceil \\frac{10+k}{2}\\right\\rceil +\\left\\lceil \\frac{29-k}{2} \\right\\rceil = 20.\\]\" width=\"214\" height=\"43\" />\nThere are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/5/e15ff9ddb9823c1cd0be7757cb01e43d4e5c6715.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20/2=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> pairs of rows, so the maximum number of students for the exam is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/f/01ff4ebe5e7dd49b03449ea217ac03451572d998.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20\\times 10=200\\rightarrow \\boxed{\\text{C}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"162\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME\" title=\"1991 AJHSME\">1991 AJHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=1991\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&